<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51249" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱστο-βοεύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆος</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>plough-tree</i> or <i>pole</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				435
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.1318
			</span></i>: prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱστοβοῆι γέροντι νέην
				ποτίβαλλε κορώνην</span> put a new tip on the old
				<i>plough</i>, of an old man marrying a young wife, Orac. ap.
				<i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				9.37.4
			</span></i>.—Acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱστοβόην</span>,
			prob. 
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱστοβοῆ</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.104
			</span></i>(<i><span class="en">
				Phil.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
